The NA62 experiment at CERN has finalized its analysis of data collected in 2016 for the $K^+ightarrow\pi^+
u ar{
u}$ decay, operating at the full design luminosity. With 181 days of data acquisition and 3.24 x 10^11 collected neutral kaon decays, a search was conducted for the $K^+ightarrow\pi^+
u ar{
u}$ decay to establish a branching ratio limit. Following data analysis, a search limit was discovered at an approximate 21% Branching Ratio at a 95% Confidence Level before considering the background contamination. Considerable improvements in sensitivity were achieved through enhanced analysis techniques and increased data volume, attaining a level 7 x 10^-11 Branching Ratio sensitivity. This improvement is primarily the result of decreased background contamination, increased data volume, and more precise particle identification methods.
